retifs on Debian, Ubuntu and Raspberry Pi OS
============================================

This is a prototype. The formats still change and the crypto awaits an
external review: keep nothing in it you can't lose.

What runs
---------
- retifsd, as a systemd user service in every user's session
  (`systemctl --user status retifsd`). Its store is ~/.local/share/retifs.
- Reticulum: retifsd needs a shared instance on the machine. If none runs
  (no rnsd, no prnsd of your own), the bundled prnsd starts with your
  config in ~/.reticulum (`systemctl --user status retifs-prnsd`).
  Out of the box it only finds others on the local network. To reach
  further, add an interface, e.g. a TCP connection to a node you trust:
      /usr/lib/retifs/prnsd interfaces add
      /usr/lib/retifs/prnsd status
  or use the retifs-desktop utility.

First steps
-----------
    retifs ping                 the daemon and this node's address
    retifs heard                public libraries announced on the network
    retifs ns join NAME ADDRESS --lazy
    retifs nodes                storage nodes heard
    retifs mount NAME           a library as files under ~/retifs/NAME

Optional services (systemctl --user enable --now ...):
    retifs-gateway              libraries as websites at http://NAME.localhost:8740/
    retifs-mount@NAME           a library mounted at login
    retifs-extractd             attributes from files (see the unit for its token)

Settings: ~/.local/share/retifs/retifs.toml (the daemon writes a commented
one at first start). Headless machines: `sudo loginctl enable-linger USER`
keeps the user services running without a login.
